  Model year 1996: position 7 is a digit, and since model year 2010 a
  passenger car must carry a letter there, so this is the 1980-2009 cycle
  (49 CFR 565.15).
  ! The check digit does not match (a check digit is mandatory only for
    vehicles sold in North America and China).

